00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.400
And I remember seeing Super Mario Bros.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:30.460
And just when you see that for the first time, I think the visuals of everything are iconic enough that it sticks with you.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.400
Because when I finally started to play Super Mario Bros.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.060
And I think the first way I played Super Mario Bros.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.240
Was actually on Super Mario All-Stars for the Super Nintendo.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.480
It was like it was already familiar to me.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.460
Even though I had never really touched it before.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:51.060
It's like it's ingrained in video game culture that in some ways or another it's already been kind of like communicated to you what Super Mario Bros.

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.580
is. Right, right.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.200
Yeah, I mean that's I think that's the experience a lot of people had too.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:57.820
It's like Super Mario is like I mean it's like Mickey Mouse.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:58.860
