00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:53.000
I think that immediately those things were kind of like shaken off.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:58.520
Right. Yeah. So I mean I actually wondered if it was going to make the essential list and even after I like first started playing it.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:08.940
I think because I had growing up I had been so used to Super Mario Brothers 3 the slight difference in the feel of it at first I kind of took as like this does feel a little outdated.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:20.180
But but kind of like you said too is as soon as I really started playing it and got into the flow of it I think I pretty early on I kicked a turtle shell at like one of the flying Koopas.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.860
And I was like oh this is fun.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.100
Like this is really fun.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:34.000
Right. And there were a lot of things like that where I just getting into the flow of it and kind of you know you get a fire flower and you're sniping you're sniping Koopas as you go.

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:43.180
And one of the biggest problems that people who have played this game in the past and revisit it one of the biggest problems they probably have is the fact that they know it all.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.140
You know right. They think they know it all.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:52.780
And there's like there's kind of like this incentive to just rush through it and you just hold down be the entire time rush through the court.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.200
I don't think that that's the way Super Mario Brothers is intended to be played.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:58.380
Right. It's fun to explore the world.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.580
And and figure it out too.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:10.320
You're going to get so many easy deaths if you just rush through this thing and don't see that Koopa that was planted at that you know like at the start of that other segment.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:18.300
You know so I think like really when you're playing this game especially because you only have three lives and that it's back to the very beginning of the game.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:26.020
You really want to make sure that you're approaching this from a standpoint of like you know that you don't know it all and that you will be surprised.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:31.480
And if you and if you don't know all the secrets and you're just running through you're going to miss some extra lives which are pretty important in this.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:38.360
Right. Yeah. I think extra lives are really key in here and it's kind of funny now that lives are in video games are like garbage.

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:40.100
Because nobody really wants them.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:48.460
But in this game they're done really well and they're done in a way that doesn't it's not so arcadey as it is kind of like a part of the experience.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:50.460
It's like a three strikes you're out kind of right.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:57.180
And the game is short enough where it doesn't bother me too much that after three strikes or after losing your life you go all the way back.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:59.860
Whereas if it was as long as Super Mario Brothers 3.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.640
Yeah. That would be crazy.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.260
Yeah. That would be a disaster.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:04.540
That would not be good.

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.520
But it's funny that you talk about it being short.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:12.660
I always thought of Super Mario Brothers as a very long game if only because I mean there's 32 levels.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:18.560
But then on top of that it's like when you do eventually die you will not make it all the way to 84 on your first run.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:23.080
It's kind of like you know in a way that's the replay value.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:30.380
It's like now you're learning to master these levels and approach them in a different way than the first time you experienced them.

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:36.180
And now you know about that Goomba in 1-2 that's going to come from the top and drop down.

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:41.100
Now you know not to be big in that particular section because you're most likely going to get hit.

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:52.140
It's funny how the game is actually pretty long just because of the way that the back to the beginning mechanic works in a way that isn't like reset frustration.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:56.640
Like it's not a oh I just lost all my lives I'm going to shut this game off now.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:58.100
I think it is kind of like you want to get back in.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:02.580
Right. And you know you might take some time in between but the next time you come back to it you're a little better at it like you said.

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:07.440
And it also has a good amount you'll discover more of the secrets along the way.

