00:59:22.080 --> 00:59:24.780
You don't like my jazzified version of the Underground song?

00:59:24.800 --> 00:59:28.420
I actually want to hear a whole album where you do stuff like that, just spoken word.

00:59:28.580 --> 00:59:29.640
Yeah, stay tuned, guys.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:34.620
Yeah, no, like the water level, that's like such a free-flowing, kind of happy tune.

00:59:34.840 --> 00:59:35.840
It's like, hey, you're underwater.

00:59:35.840 --> 00:59:40.080
It's funny because that song, it doesn't deserve that.

00:59:40.140 --> 00:59:41.000
I get it.

00:59:41.080 --> 00:59:42.000
I know what you're saying.

00:59:42.100 --> 00:59:43.180
It does sound like it's underwater.

00:59:43.440 --> 00:59:47.060
It doesn't deserve that because the underwater levels are the most frustrating part of the game.

00:59:47.180 --> 00:59:49.280
No, the underwater levels suck.

00:59:49.300 --> 00:59:51.460
And that music starts to taunt you after a while.

00:59:51.600 --> 00:59:54.420
Yeah, but that's part of it, why it's so good.

00:59:54.540 --> 01:00:00.700
Part of the reason why the underwater levels suck is because they take away the best mechanic

01:00:00.700 --> 01:00:01.660
of the game.

01:00:01.740 --> 01:00:04.940
The jump is gone and replaced with this info-jump.

01:00:04.940 --> 01:00:09.580
And I don't really think that feels that well, controlling the info-jump, as I call it.

01:00:09.780 --> 01:00:10.800
Because here's why.

01:00:11.200 --> 01:00:14.240
Sometimes you hit that button and you can go pretty far up.

01:00:14.380 --> 01:00:16.580
Other times he does like this half-step.

01:00:16.760 --> 01:00:18.260
Yeah. And he just keeps falling.

01:00:18.400 --> 01:00:22.820
This would be fine, you know, if you were trying to simulate like the roughness of the ocean or something.

01:00:23.080 --> 01:00:26.800
But it's not fine when you have bloopers all over you, okay?

01:00:26.800 --> 01:00:28.680
I'm cool with the Cheep Cheeps coming by.

01:00:29.020 --> 01:00:30.880
Cheep Cheeps. That's what they're called.

01:00:30.880 --> 01:00:33.880
I know, but just the words that you're saying and then the info-jump.

01:00:34.140 --> 01:00:35.180
Yeah. And you know what?

01:00:35.240 --> 01:00:37.040
There's a lot. This is Super Mario slang.

01:00:37.360 --> 01:00:40.060
Okay? This is like the kids know about this stuff.

01:00:40.120 --> 01:00:42.760
Yeah. Okay? And Cheep Cheeps are like, they're fine.

01:00:42.900 --> 01:00:44.580
They're kind of like this thing that just floats by.

01:00:44.820 --> 01:00:45.900
You know, take them or leave them.

01:00:46.240 --> 01:00:48.920
They're pretty easy obstacles to avoid.

01:00:49.340 --> 01:00:50.480
Bloopers. They go after you.

01:00:50.580 --> 01:00:51.940
These guys are like, yeah, but you know what?

01:00:51.940 --> 01:00:56.300
Not only do they go after you, but if you stay in a particular spot, right, they just

01:00:56.300 --> 01:00:58.140
kind of like, they like wait.

01:00:58.400 --> 01:01:00.060
They like hover right around that same spot.

01:01:00.140 --> 01:01:01.540
They're not going to keep floating around.

01:01:01.640 --> 01:01:03.920
They're not going to float toward you. They just wait for you.

01:01:04.040 --> 01:01:07.700
And it's like next to Hammer Brothers, next to Hammer Brothers, they're some of the most

01:01:07.700 --> 01:01:08.860
vicious enemies in the game.

01:01:09.620 --> 01:01:10.600
Really not a fan of bloopers.

01:01:10.780 --> 01:01:12.500
Really not a fan of the info-jump.

01:01:12.720 --> 01:01:18.200
And water levels in general just like distarts that notion that water levels are garbage.

01:01:18.620 --> 01:01:21.100
You know, like this is, when did we had a, think about it.

01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:24.460
In all the other NES launch games, was there a water level?

01:01:24.980 --> 01:01:28.560
No. You could argue Klu Klu Land takes place underwater.

01:01:30.740 --> 01:01:33.360
But that definitely didn't control like a water game.

01:01:33.540 --> 01:01:36.740
Like I never, well, maybe actually now that you think about it, maybe that's why those

01:01:36.740 --> 01:01:37.640
turns are so slippery.

01:01:38.040 --> 01:01:39.800
I mean, that's not how I move underwater.

01:01:40.080 --> 01:01:42.440
It's not how you move because you're not bubbles.

01:01:42.880 --> 01:01:45.740
That's true. Yeah, moving along here.

01:01:46.360 --> 01:01:47.600
So we were talking about the music.

01:01:47.960 --> 01:01:50.040
So Sam said his favorite is underwater.

01:01:50.040 --> 01:01:51.740
Sean, you said underground.

01:01:54.120 --> 01:01:56.400
Guys, I'm having a little bit of a stroke here right now.

01:01:56.600 --> 01:01:57.560
If you want me to sing it again.

01:01:57.640 --> 01:01:58.640
I don't think I want to say this again.

01:01:58.760 --> 01:01:59.820
I think I'm going to just.

01:01:59.820 --> 01:02:00.740
Yeah, what's your favorite, Mike?

01:02:00.760 --> 01:02:02.260
Thank you so much for asking me.

01:02:02.480 --> 01:02:05.820
And I'm going to be boring and say that it is the overworld theme just because.

01:02:06.060 --> 01:02:07.840
You're so basic. Well, here's why though.

01:02:07.940 --> 01:02:09.100
It's such a good theme. Yeah.

01:02:09.260 --> 01:02:11.540
The other themes have all stayed with us too, right?

01:02:11.680 --> 01:02:13.580
So it's like we never lost the underwater theme.

01:02:13.680 --> 01:02:15.640
You can still hear that in new Super Mario Brothers games.

01:02:15.640 --> 01:02:20.880
We didn't even lose the dungeon theme, I guess I'll call it, for like the fourth level of each world.

01:02:21.360 --> 01:02:23.240
I mean, that's pretty spooky too.

01:02:23.440 --> 01:02:28.200
Yeah. But the thing about the overworld is it's synonymous with Mario now.

01:02:28.360 --> 01:02:29.920
Like you can't have anybody not.

01:02:30.020 --> 01:02:33.200
And everybody has like their own lyrics to it too, which is kind of weird.

01:02:33.280 --> 01:02:37.660
I always associate it with do the Mario, which is part of the Super Mario Brothers Super Show.

01:02:37.660 --> 01:02:42.280
But like I've seen other versions where, and maybe this is something that just was done earlier,

01:02:42.540 --> 01:02:48.020
but people had like a lyrical pattern to the song to sing about Mario.

01:02:48.020 --> 01:02:52.780
And it's just like, it's just neat that like people hear this song and they immediately think of Mario.

01:02:52.900 --> 01:02:57.680
I can't think of actually like a more iconic song for video games.

01:02:58.420 --> 01:03:03.520
Not like, wow, Stairway to Heaven or Super Mario Brothers overworld theme.

01:03:03.900 --> 01:03:05.520
You know, I guess you could argue.

01:03:05.520 --> 01:03:08.760
I would argue that more people know the Mario than Stairway to Heaven.

01:03:08.880 --> 01:03:09.780
You know what? I would say so.

01:03:09.900 --> 01:03:12.200
It sounds about right actually if you think about it.

01:03:12.380 --> 01:03:16.820
But I mean like what other kind of video game themes are there that are like that level?

01:03:17.100 --> 01:03:20.440
You know, there's a lot of other Nintendo games, I guess.

01:03:20.580 --> 01:03:25.000
Like Zelda has, you know, like what would you, what would Zelda song would you pick?

01:03:25.080 --> 01:03:28.520
I'd probably do the. Yeah, I think it would be that overworld theme too.

01:03:28.760 --> 01:03:30.440
Some people might say it's the menu music.

01:03:30.460 --> 01:03:33.140
What about the battle music from Shin Megami Tensei IV?

01:03:33.460 --> 01:03:35.300
You know what? I can't believe, screw it.

01:03:35.300 --> 01:03:36.780
That's actually, that's the answer.

01:03:38.340 --> 01:03:41.840
Now are you talking about Shin Megami Tensei IV or Shin Megami Tensei IV Apocalypse?

01:03:42.920 --> 01:03:44.220
Four. Okay, yeah.

01:03:44.800 --> 01:03:46.800
Some people might say Apocalypse is the definitive version.

01:03:47.320 --> 01:03:51.820
I'll tell you what, Super Mario overworld theme is definitely the definitive Mario song for me.

01:03:51.920 --> 01:03:55.600
I would say like in gaming also, like the Halo theme is big.

01:03:55.800 --> 01:03:57.540
But Mario isn't just in gaming.

01:03:57.720 --> 01:04:00.180
Like you don't have to know anything about games to know the Mario song.

01:04:00.180 --> 01:04:02.760
Yeah, you just heard the song somewhere regardless.

01:04:03.080 --> 01:04:17.840
Yeah. It's funny that this game turns Mario into a mascot for Nintendo.

01:04:17.840 --> 01:04:22.780
But at this point, Mario's like, he might even be more notable if you think about it than Mickey Mouse.

01:04:22.880 --> 01:04:23.740
And here's why I'm going to say that.

01:04:23.920 --> 01:04:25.820
Because they don't use Mickey Mouse that often.

01:04:26.020 --> 01:04:28.980
Like he's the face of Disney if you think about it.

01:04:29.060 --> 01:04:33.020
But when was the last time there was like a Mickey movie or something like that?

01:04:33.020 --> 01:04:40.420
You know, like Mickey is now, I think like Mickey isn't as welcomed as Mario is if he really, I mean like, I don't want to get into a whole debate here.

01:04:40.620 --> 01:04:46.500
But am I wrong to think that like if a Mickey Mouse movie comes out tomorrow, it's not necessarily going to be a great movie.

01:04:46.580 --> 01:04:49.960
If a Mario Brothers game comes out tomorrow, it's probably going to be a pretty good game.

01:04:50.200 --> 01:04:51.000
Well, here's my.

01:04:51.060 --> 01:04:51.880
Okay, go ahead.

01:04:52.020 --> 01:04:53.680
Okay, here's my thing with that.

01:04:53.960 --> 01:04:57.180
Mickey Mouse is weird, but pretends he's not weird, right?

01:04:57.800 --> 01:04:59.640
Mario is like, it's me, Mario.

01:04:59.640 --> 01:05:03.740
You know, like he knows it's a weird thing, there's mushrooms everywhere, and he just owns it.

01:05:04.020 --> 01:05:05.760
That's my dispute with Mickey.

01:05:05.940 --> 01:05:15.140
I want to say that I think just because Mickey Mouse has had about 100 years or so to develop brand awareness,

01:05:15.560 --> 01:05:25.780
I would say that while Nintendo gets a hell of a lot more utility out of Mario, I think that, I think Mickey still has him beat.

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:27.840
Okay. And that's what we need.

01:05:27.840 --> 01:05:30.160
We need a devil's advocate on this show.

01:05:30.300 --> 01:05:31.400
I'm not being a devil's advocate.

01:05:31.540 --> 01:05:35.980
That's just what I feel. We need a guy who hates Mario and is probably going to vote him out of the essential games list.

01:05:36.180 --> 01:05:37.020
You know, we just need.

01:05:37.160 --> 01:05:38.020
You never know, Mike.

01:05:38.180 --> 01:05:40.540
Everybody needs a dark wizard Koopa.

01:05:40.880 --> 01:05:43.200
Dark wizard. I believe it's sorcerer.

01:05:43.380 --> 01:05:45.140
I'm pretty sure they refer to him as a sorcerer.

01:05:45.360 --> 01:05:48.320
Okay. Well, it's funny that you mentioned that, or I mentioned it, I guess.

01:05:48.540 --> 01:05:53.140
It's funny that. It's funny that I mentioned that because this is going to segue great into the next fact I have to bring up,

01:05:53.140 --> 01:06:01.340
which is that Bowser in the Japanese version is actually referred to as the great demon king Koopa.

01:06:01.820 --> 01:06:03.520
Like, that's pretty, that's pretty dope.

01:06:03.820 --> 01:06:07.260
It's pretty metal. Like, I would be afraid to fight the great demon king.

01:06:07.460 --> 01:06:09.520
I know the Japanese have a thing with demons.

01:06:09.520 --> 01:06:16.980
Like, if you notice in video games in general, like, the last boss of any JRPG is usually, like, either a god or a demon.

01:06:17.200 --> 01:06:20.420
They kind of got a weird thing for, like, Christian symbolism.

01:06:20.840 --> 01:06:27.600
Like, it's not that, like, they really, they're, like, afraid of it or they find it very, very meaningful.

01:06:27.600 --> 01:06:28.900
They just kind of dig it.

01:06:29.200 --> 01:06:33.180
Like, they just like, like, demons and Bibles and stuff like that.

01:06:33.180 --> 01:06:39.500
I don't know about you guys, but even in this stage of Mario's, like, infancy, I wouldn't associate Bowser as a demon.

01:06:39.920 --> 01:06:43.720
No. Like, you know, like, they, they, he's definitely, he's a very bad turtle.

01:06:43.940 --> 01:06:46.940
Yeah, I mean, and they've, you know, cuddled him down a lot.

01:06:47.120 --> 01:06:51.860
Like, he's now kind of, like, this cute, adorable, fat thing that Mario fights occasionally.

01:06:52.260 --> 01:06:55.960
But, like, in this game, he still has, like, a pretty terrifying presence.

01:06:56.440 --> 01:07:01.520
But before we get into the, you know, the great big bad at the end, I just want to talk about some of the other enemies.

01:07:01.520 --> 01:07:05.840
So, we talked about, you know, like, some guys very, like, very quickly.

01:07:06.220 --> 01:07:07.940
But I just want to get your thoughts, all right?

01:07:07.940 --> 01:07:10.900
This is not like a, let's break down the Goomba.

01:07:10.920 --> 01:07:12.240
Okay? I don't want to do that.

01:07:12.660 --> 01:07:13.940
But yeah, just give me a couple words per guy.

01:07:14.060 --> 01:07:14.920
I'd love to hear your thoughts.

01:07:14.920 --> 01:07:16.580
And this, I think this could be fun if we do it right.

01:07:16.800 --> 01:07:19.460
Yeah. Okay? So, Sean, Goombas.

01:07:19.800 --> 01:07:21.620
Squishy. Ooh, that's, that's a good one.

01:07:21.920 --> 01:07:23.300
Sam, what do you got? I got Jump.

01:07:23.600 --> 01:07:24.680
That's, that's it. Jump.

01:07:24.940 --> 01:07:26.580
Could you associate, like, squashing them?

01:07:26.700 --> 01:07:30.880
Yeah, like the first, like the first level, they got that one Goomba that just, you know,

01:07:30.880 --> 01:07:35.400
shows you, like, listen, you got to jump over this guy or jump on him in order to get by.

01:07:35.520 --> 01:07:36.400
And that's just what I think.

01:07:36.640 --> 01:07:37.660
My thoughts on Goombas?

01:07:37.980 --> 01:07:38.920
Harmless. Okay?

01:07:39.280 --> 01:07:42.980
These guys couldn't, couldn't do anything to Mario if we really think about the situation.

01:07:43.220 --> 01:07:44.820
Like, if you don't, if you don't jump.

01:07:45.080 --> 01:07:49.980
No, no, no. I, I'm saying, like, the way that I always think about Goombas is, like, to me, they were

01:07:49.980 --> 01:07:52.260
that reference point of most useless enemy.

01:07:52.260 --> 01:07:56.180
Mm-hmm. Now, I'm not, I'm not denying that in Super Mario Brothers, they will kill you a lot.

01:07:56.480 --> 01:08:00.480
But I'm saying, if we're really looking at this Koopa tribe and what he's sending at

01:08:00.480 --> 01:08:04.020
us, the Goombas are, like, the least of our worries, you know?

01:08:04.180 --> 01:08:08.920
And it's just funny that they don't have arms, they just have these shoes, and they just,

01:08:08.980 --> 01:08:11.940
like, walk around and waddle, and it's just, it's very strange.

01:08:12.380 --> 01:08:13.760
Okay. Koopa Troopa, Sean.

01:08:13.980 --> 01:08:15.420
So this is just the walking one.

01:08:15.480 --> 01:08:16.380
Just the walking one.

01:08:16.380 --> 01:08:18.280
We got a special name for the flying ones.

01:08:19.780 --> 01:08:21.120
Just talk to me about it.

01:08:21.220 --> 01:08:25.740
I mean, he, these ones actually get me a lot more.

01:08:26.260 --> 01:08:28.560
I hate, well, they all get me a lot.

01:08:28.760 --> 01:08:34.800
I'm really, again, I'm really bad at the game, but I would say that I have been terrorized

01:08:34.800 --> 01:08:36.440
by, they get me.

01:08:36.660 --> 01:08:37.980
They get you. No, they get me, too.

01:08:37.980 --> 01:08:40.960
I've been terrorized by Koopa Troopas more than my fair share.

01:08:41.200 --> 01:08:43.380
Yeah. That's about, that's about on par for me.

01:08:43.380 --> 01:08:48.820
Yeah, I think the funny thing about a Koopa Troopa is that they don't get me in the sense

01:08:48.820 --> 01:08:53.420
that, like, I run into them as much as I might run into a Goomba, but they get me when I hit

01:08:53.420 --> 01:08:58.420
them on the shell, and then they accidentally, like, come back the other way, and that's

01:08:58.420 --> 01:08:59.760
frustrating. Oh, yeah.

01:08:59.980 --> 01:09:03.760
Very. Okay, so now, Sean, Koopa Paratroopas.

01:09:04.120 --> 01:09:05.380
We don't talk about those.

01:09:05.880 --> 01:09:10.180
I feel like those are, I like those in that you can use them for platforming, and sometimes

01:09:10.180 --> 01:09:13.260
you have to, and I think that that's, like, a cool way of taking out enemies.

01:09:13.380 --> 01:09:17.840
I like that you mentioned that because you can use them for platforming, and they usually

01:09:17.840 --> 01:09:21.380
get you up to, like, a higher platform if you time the jump right, but you're also, like,

01:09:21.400 --> 01:09:22.260
you're not punished.

01:09:22.440 --> 01:09:25.880
There's no, like, hit this Koopa Troopa, or you're falling into the pit.

01:09:25.980 --> 01:09:27.620
Well, in some later levels, aren't they?

01:09:27.620 --> 01:09:30.780
I meant, like, if you hit it, if you don't hit it at exactly the right time, like, even

01:09:30.780 --> 01:09:34.460
if you move forward, you'll still be able to land on something.

01:09:34.860 --> 01:09:39.380
Obviously, like, below, directly below the Koopa Troopa, Koopa Paratroopa would be a pit.

01:09:39.620 --> 01:09:41.840
Right. But nothing, like, yonder.

01:09:42.640 --> 01:09:44.960
Over yonder. So that's nice.

01:09:44.980 --> 01:09:48.660
It's not, like, so punishing, but it rewards the player if they can time it right.

01:09:48.840 --> 01:09:49.860
For me... Real quick. Yeah.

01:09:50.240 --> 01:09:52.080
What's the difference between the green ones and the red ones?

01:09:52.160 --> 01:09:54.520
So the green ones always just continue to move forward.

01:09:54.680 --> 01:09:56.140
Red ones stay on their platforms.

01:09:56.380 --> 01:10:01.860
Okay, cool. So if, yeah, they'll continue to walk back and forth, even if there's not a block to tell

01:10:01.860 --> 01:10:04.240
them to go the other way, they won't fall off the cliff.

01:10:04.380 --> 01:10:06.340
That makes the Super Smash Brothers shells make more sense.

01:10:06.480 --> 01:10:09.080
Yes. But they're also just, like, they're just intelligent, I guess.

01:10:09.160 --> 01:10:10.280
Like, the red ones have evolved.

01:10:10.280 --> 01:10:13.100
Like, hey, wait, if I fall off of this platform, I can die.

01:10:13.240 --> 01:10:14.240
Right. And they just learned.

01:10:14.240 --> 01:10:18.560
And so the green ones remain stupid, and they only mate with the other stupid green ones.

01:10:18.660 --> 01:10:21.540
And the red ones, you know, have evolved to a higher society.

01:10:22.100 --> 01:10:27.460
For me, Koopa Paratroopers, real fast, Koopa Paratroopers, I can't time them correctly.

01:10:27.880 --> 01:10:32.420
Whenever I think that I should jump to get on top of them, they jump with me, and then

01:10:32.420 --> 01:10:33.840
we collide, and it's stupid.

01:10:34.060 --> 01:10:38.680
But how come on that death screen, the Koopa Paratroopers don't also die?

01:10:38.680 --> 01:10:40.780
How about anything you run into for that matter?

01:10:40.940 --> 01:10:44.900
Like, if it kills me by walking into it, why aren't they hurt at all?

01:10:45.060 --> 01:10:46.240
Because you know what, Mike?

01:10:46.400 --> 01:10:49.120
Like, this is your fault.

01:10:49.340 --> 01:10:51.140
No one said the Mushroom Kingdom was going to be fair.

01:10:51.140 --> 01:10:53.140
Yeah, exactly. It's your failing.

01:10:53.340 --> 01:10:56.260
I just think that, you know, there should be a game theory on that.

01:10:56.520 --> 01:10:58.480
Yeah. Okay.

01:10:59.320 --> 01:11:00.200
Buzzy Beetle.

01:11:00.500 --> 01:11:01.340
Do you know who that is?

01:11:01.480 --> 01:11:03.120
Oh, yeah. That's the little helmet dudes.

01:11:03.460 --> 01:11:08.600
Yeah. Which is really cool that you mentioned helmet dudes, because in Super Mario Maker, which

01:11:08.600 --> 01:11:12.880
comes out 30 years later in this game, you can wear them as helmets.

01:11:13.120 --> 01:11:16.020
Unfortunately, not a design concept in Super Mario Brothers.

01:11:17.020 --> 01:11:19.780
Yeah. And their thing is that they can't get hit by fireballs.

01:11:19.920 --> 01:11:21.720
Which I think is nice. I think it's cool.

01:11:21.840 --> 01:11:25.320
It's cool that, like, not every enemy can just be destroyed with the click of a button.

01:11:25.840 --> 01:11:26.840
A click? Yeah.

01:11:26.940 --> 01:11:27.960
Are you clicking? Oh, okay.

01:11:28.100 --> 01:11:28.920
Click your B button. Yeah.

01:11:29.060 --> 01:11:32.000
Okay. I'm sorry. I guess, like, it's press is the right word.

01:11:32.180 --> 01:11:33.640
But, yeah, I think, like, click works here.

01:11:33.920 --> 01:11:34.940
Okay. Buzzy Beetle thoughts?

01:11:35.520 --> 01:11:36.600
No. Okay.

01:11:36.700 --> 01:11:39.580
Wow. Never really. You never have any dreams about the Buzzy Beetles.

01:11:40.240 --> 01:11:43.060
All right. So then let's move on to these guys are really tough.

