01:21:27.220 --> 01:21:28.020
That's really cool.

01:21:28.140 --> 01:21:30.240
In fact, I'd go as far as saying that that's metal.

01:21:30.400 --> 01:21:31.360
That's so metal.

01:21:31.420 --> 01:21:35.020
That's so metal of you to get through the whole game like that.

01:21:35.160 --> 01:21:41.780
And that's probably the way a lot of people who are real NES players who played this console day in and day out

01:21:41.780 --> 01:21:45.720
throughout the console's lifespan, that's probably how they beat this game multiple times.

01:21:46.040 --> 01:21:52.720
But with today's standards of games and being used to some kind of save state

01:21:52.720 --> 01:21:55.620
or being able to start at least at the beginning of the world,

01:21:55.620 --> 01:21:57.620
I just don't think it's very fair to say,

